    {
      "id": "overlay",
      "title": "T and R overlaid, at rest",
      "caption": "The same colours as the turn: green alpha 1 beta 1, blue alpha 2 beta 2, beta the lighter shade. Solid: R. Faded: the T position of alpha 2 beta 2. Alpha 1 beta 1 is drawn once, in R, because it matches the T pair to 0.9 \u00c5 RMS over 285 alpha-carbon atoms. With it fitted, alpha 2 beta 2 in R is turned 14.1 degrees about one axis and shifted 1.3 \u00c5 along it. Its alpha carbons lie 5.2 \u00c5 RMS from their T positions.",
